Z||000000||Beaverman||03-14-2001||09:37 PM||||Got a few more questions for you motor types.  Okay test drove that 87 GT tonight and the oil gauge after you drive it and stop it wants to red light and kinda go down.  At the same time the tach is jumping a lil.  Also when I turned it off.  and tried to turn it back on it kinda seemed like it didn't want to start. Any ideas? Advise would be nice hencing i'm buying it tommorow if its not any hard fixes.  The tach/oil thing only does it at idle...could it be a short perhaps in a wire...and the tach filter.?<P>Thanks<P>Jesse<p>[This message has been edited by Beaverman (edited 03-14-2001).]||||reg||11
Z||000001||GoCartGuy||03-14-2001||09:53 PM||||Ok, I know all the motor heads will probably laugh at me for this but hey here's my reply posting.  First off, on your tach jumping a bit, there was an earlier post this week, I think they mentioned the filter as a possible source of the problem, but I don't remember, run a search on it.  This could also be the source of the oil pressure problem.  Could also be the wrong weight or in need of a change.  As far as the hard to restart problem, had the same trouble with my 85 GT, turns out the battery wasn't holding a decent charge, it was ancient...a $40 fix.  <P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||1
Z||000002||Beaverman||03-14-2001||09:57 PM||||Ya i'll be definatelly replacing the tach filter.  The guy seemed to think it was in the wiring that goes to the distributor cap.  Just i hadn't drove it back at the other post and the oil thing kinda annoyed me.  It was almost like it was surging.  Will definatelly try a new battery or a different battery.  Thanks :P||||reg||1
